 irregular-shaped black molten mass is formed at the end of the wire, and a green powder-like substance is attached to the surface.\n\nHotspots:\n\n*   ID 1: \\[100, 380, 250, 500] (Top center melted part) - \"Irregular spherical melting marks formed at the end of the wire and green oxide attached. The boundary with the surrounding conductor is clear, and a sudden phase change is suspected.\"\n*   ID 2: \\[350, 750, 580, 950] (Right charred junction) - \"The original shape is lost due to the concentrated carbonization of the cable sheath and internal insulation, and a porous carbonized material is formed. It is judged to be the point with the highest concentration of heat flow.\"\n*Quality Assessment:* The resolution is good, but the contrast is somewhat low to grasp the internal texture of the carbonized part. Recommend applying a high-contrast filter and close-up shooting to check the microstructure.\n\nThat's a solid, objective analysis of the scene. Now, on to the next one...", "will_print_thinking": true}, "timestamp": 1767661232935}
