 image quality is good overall, but some fine details of the melted masses are a bit blurred.\n\nHotspots. I'm identifying two primary hotspots. The first is the bulbous blackened mass at the top. The reason is the distinct morphological change – swelling and melting – compared to the rest of the wire. The second hotspot is the junction where the wires emerge from cable ②. The rationale is the highest concentration of charred residue and loss of insulation integrity.\n\nFor image quality, the brightness is adequate, and the sharpness is decent for general viewing. However, we're lacking macro-level detail on the melted areas. A suggestion would be to use macro photography to get a closer look at those melted ends and adjust the contrast to better differentiate between the black char and the dark shadows.\n\nFinally, a quick constraint check: \"Short circuit\"? Nope. \"Arc\"? No. \"Overload\"? Not a chance.", "will_print_thinking": true}, "timestamp": 1767661685561}
