aged insulation tells a story. Then, the Cable ② termination is the second, because this area displays the most severe thermal damage and mass loss. Third, I have identified a greenish oxidation area, as it is a visual indicator of chemical changes and oxidation in the copper.\n\nFinally, the **Image Quality Assessment** is performed. The brightness is adequate. The sharpness, however, is moderate; some areas are slightly out of focus. To improve this, I'm recommending a higher resolution for macro shots of the copper ends and applying sharpening filters. This will reveal finer surface textures.\n\nI've ensured to stick to the parameters - there's no mention of \"short circuits\" or \"arcs\" or any other causal inference. It's all about what's visible: shape, color, location, size, and texture, all in the prescribed format. My aim is a professional, unbiased, and technically sound assessment, and that's what I've delivered. The final JSON output will reflect this meticulous process.", "will_print_thinking": true}, "timestamp": 1767661876263}
